{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792715331,"nonce":"g5+7LUa1gOMYSsa/SpQi+pBNHgU=","message":"Implemented native canvas retention under an open static owner. The walker invokes dynamic callbacks during the owning group paint even when skip_canvas_drawing is set, and omits those callbacks from separate canvas overlay records and Canvas dynamic regions. Their native shapes, path meshes, raw RGBA and auxiliary rows stay beside sibling draws and ancestor commands.\n\nRenderTree keeps a retained-canvas flag with full-paint lifetime. The app invalidates compositor replay while the flag is set and rejects primitive-splice replay before invoking callbacks. Nested retained content uses existing ordered single-sample background dispatch. Foreground replay already uses the owning ordered stream. The redraw bookkeeping includes retained callbacks even with an empty overlay registry. The flag clears when the group no longer retains the callback or the owner becomes unpainted. Independent canvases still collect normally.\n\nNegative control: first compositor frame, background static ancestor opacity 0.5, red static sibling and green RGBA canvas. Pixel (55,55) was [64,128,64,255], expected isolated [0,128,127,255]. The ownership/cache wiring fixed that control. Expanded tests preserve nested opacity endpoint commands and prevent loss of the redraw signal after callbacks leave the independent overlay registry. One initial expanded-test compile failed because Canvas has no id builder; the fixture now checks the record/region collections directly. No production compile failure remained.\n\nScoped validation, CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2, offscreen Metal, capacities 1024:\n- cargo test -p blinc_app retained_canvas --lib -- --include-ignored --test-threads=1: three pass in storage and three pass with vertex storage/storage buffers forced off. Two GPU controls and one CPU producer/metadata control.\n- Public direct/compositor frames cover both native background and foreground ancestors, changed RGBA pixels, shapes, empty output and recovery, triangular path clips plus rectangular scissors, nested opacity 1 -\u003e 0.5 -\u003e 0 -\u003e 0.75 -\u003e 1, and a tessellated triangle overlapping a sibling shape. Later frames are cache eligible. Callback counters show exactly one invocation per frame for both retained and unrelated canvases. Retained metadata, commands and visible redraw signals are asserted, including empty output. Background and foreground nested command arrays remain four entries with the directed opacity.\n- The CPU control checks skip_canvas_drawing retention, command ownership, unflattened child alpha, path auxiliary rows, absence of an independent Canvas region, and flag/record reset when the owner stops grouping or becomes transparent.\n- Existing rgba_order_canvas_frames_preserve_visit_order_updates_and_foreground_meshes and foreground_rgba_application_frames_update_pixels_then_shapes_then_empty pass in storage, one case each. These preserve ordinary independent callback output/order.\n- Touched Rust files only: rustfmt and diff checks pass. Capability overrides restored. No workspace, DSL, docs, platform or unrelated gates.\n\nLogs: /private/tmp/blinc-retained-canvas-{negative,wiring,controls,normal-rgba-order,normal-foreground-rgba,dt-app}.log.\n\nCosts/limits: one per-tree flag; no GPU layout/shader change or new per-canvas texture mechanism. Visible retained canvases conservatively force a full walk/cache repaint even when their output is unchanged. Existing group texture pooling/ordered dispatch is reused. No timing/memory benchmark, mobile/browser, scheduler interpolation or new glass/3D effect claim. Cross-background/foreground callbacks, dynamic/composite ancestor owners, separate GPU passes/3D meshes, text/SVG/ImageElement streams, named Sample and general opacity flattening remain outside this child on e0a7502. Nothing pushed.","files":null}]}